PROMPT

Create one full-body, production-ready 2D boss sprite for the Urkaaaz Android
siege game: a massive stone-and-root guardian that serves as the mobile siege
boss for the Chapter 1 finale.

Use the attached selected concept as the character's source of truth. Keep the
colossus's broad, forward-leaning rocky body, massive rounded boulder fists,
root-and-vine joints, thick leafy shoulders and canopy, crooked branching
crown, and single bright amber eye. Retain the threatening, slightly
grotesque expression and imposing silhouette. It should read as a living
mobile siege creature, not a human wearing armor and not a conventional treant.

The attached preview's checkerboard is an editing artifact, not artwork.
Recreate the character cleanly and leave every pixel outside its silhouette
transparent. Preserve the existing face and body design; do not invent a
different boss, weapon, shell, tower, shield, or companion.

Use the Ancient War Oak frame as the rendering-style reference: painterly
fantasy-game surfaces, textured stone and foliage, clear material separation,
controlled highlights, and readable forms. Give this boss its own identity:
rock and root anatomy, broad fists, leafy crown, and amber eye must remain
distinct from the Oak's tree trunk and branch silhouette.

Compose the sprite in a stable three-quarter frontal view facing left toward
the BLUE fortress. Keep the complete crown, shoulders, fists, legs, and feet
visible. The feet rest on a clean, level gameplay baseline; the body and
crown fill roughly the same vertical world-space footprint as the existing
Thorncrown sprite. Keep the amber eye and fist silhouettes recognizable at
small match-screen scale.

Render only the boss sprite. Do not draw a battlefield, forest, ground plane,
cast shadow, background glow, impact effect, health bar, HUD, name, text, logo,
or additional character. Do not add a floor or scenery to explain the pose.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

- Output exactly one PNG named `green_frontier_chapter1_final_boss.png`.
- Canvas: exactly 1145 × 1374 pixels, portrait, RGBA.
- Use genuine alpha transparency outside the complete character. No
  checkerboard, matte, flat background color, or opaque border.
- Preserve the selected concept's identity and facing direction while fitting
  the technical sprite canvas; do not stretch the image to convert its
  landscape preview into portrait.
- Keep all crown branches, fists, and feet inside the canvas with a small
  transparent safety margin. Preserve a clear, stable bottom baseline.
- Save the review output to
  `assets_src/bosses/green_frontier_chapter1_final_boss.png`.
  Do not overwrite or delete the current Thorncrown runtime asset.
- This is one static sprite, not an animation, sprite sheet, contact sheet, or
  gameplay screenshot.

